issue_comments.body:
@Col-5555 Thanks for the detailed reproduction and the distinction between the winner cache and sparse-MLA calibration. The managed-cache reload here does not synchronize the CPB/crossover side file, so I agree that identical winner entries alone do not establish identical sparse-kernel selection.

The pending refresh documents that boundary and the pre-calibrate/reuse approach via FLASHINFER_AUTOTUNE_DIR. It also temporarily retains legacy behavior for multi-rank deployments while the separate cache-hit race is fixed in flashinfer-ai/flashinfer#6185. That gate does not solve the calibration distribution issue you describe.

Please share your patch, especially the process-cache installation step. A supported FlashInfer calibration export/install API looks preferable to having vLLM depend on private cache globals; we should validate that separately on the affected SM120 topology. I am not including an unvalidated side-file broadcast in this cache-lifecycle refresh.
